  "prompt_template": "You are configuring a self-hosted homelab from junk drawers and old hardware.\n\nUser Hardware:\n{{selected_hardware}}\n\nUser Goals:\n{{selected_goals}}\n\nNetwork Setup:\n{{network_capabilities}}\n\nBased on 'Junk Drawer Homelab' chapters 4-16, recommend:\n1. Which chapters to build\n2. Which hardware runs each chapter\n3. Build order\n4. Gotchas and conflicts\n\nRespond as JSON:\n{\n  \"recommended_chapters\": [4, 5, ...],\n  \"hardware_assignments\": {\"4\": \"pi4\", \"5\": \"laptop\", ...},\n  \"build_order\": [4, 8, 5, 9, ...],\n  \"warnings\": [\"Pi-hole must be always-on\", ...],\n  \"subscriptions_saved\": \"Netflix, Disney+, Google One, Bitwarden, ...\"\n}\n\nKey insights:\n- Pi-hole (Ch 4): DNS filtering, minimal resources, always-on\n- Jellyfin (Ch 5): Media transcoding \u2192 Intel Quick Sync (8th-gen+) or fast CPU\n- Immich (Ch 7): Photo ML search \u2192 4GB+ RAM, GPU helps\n- Ollama (Ch 13): LOCAL LLM inference \u2192 GPU essential (NVIDIA CUDA > AMD ROCm > CPU)\n- Tailscale (Ch 10): Remote access without port forwarding\n- Home Assistant (Ch 14) + MCP: AI automation, depends on stable always-on\n- n8n (Ch 15): Workflow automation (replaces Zapier, IFTTT)\n- Proxmox (Ch 16): Cluster last (needs 3+ x86 machines with 16GB+ RAM each)\n"
